                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73236242-2e62-4ff5-8144-69e2d2b5ccdb",
                                                "sense_id": "cff2c3b7-109c-38a4-9f27-f846be6abbc5",
                                                "text": "Thus the condition of quadruplicate tetrasomy, triplicate hexasomy, in the apple, and probably several other data of the literature would deserve a statistical treatment according to Propach’s procedure before attaining classical significance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b698e1fd-6dab-4c8f-abd3-4d8e69204fe8",
                                                "sense_id": "cff2c3b7-109c-38a4-9f27-f846be6abbc5",
                                                "text": "sSMC are scientifically interesting due to their still not completely understood mode of formation, karyotypic evolution and the fact, that their presence may lead to chromosomal imbalances (partial tri-, tetra- or hexasomies) without detectable clinical consequences."
